**Outbound headers** (all set in this file):

- **`r.Out.Host`** is set in the `Rewrite` func of `ServeHTTP`:
  ```go
  if rp.socketPath != "" {
      r.Out.Host = rp.url.Host
  } else {
      r.Out.Host = r.In.Host
  }
  ```

- **`X-Forwarded-Host`, `X-Forwarded-Proto`, `X-Forwarded-For`** are set in `addProxyForwardedHeaders`:
  ```go
  r.Out.Header.Set("X-Forwarded-Host", r.In.Host)
  if r.In.TLS != nil {
      r.Out.Header.Set("X-Forwarded-Proto", "https")
  }
  if c, ok := serveHTTPContextKey.ValueOk(r.Out.Context()); ok {
      r.Out.Header.Set("X-Forwarded-For", c.SrcAddr.Addr().String())
  }
  ```

- **`Tailscale-User-Login`** is set in `addTailscaleIdentityHeaders`:
  ```go
  r.Out.Header.Set("Tailscale-User-Login", encTailscaleHeaderValue(user.LoginName))
  ```
  This runs only if `WhoIs` succeeds and the node is not tagged. Incoming copies of the header are deleted first by `delHeaderVariants`.

- **`Tailscale-Funnel-Request`** is set for funneled traffic:
  ```go
  if c.Funnel != nil {
      r.Out.Header.Set("Tailscale-Funnel-Request", "?1")
      return
  }
  ```

**Streaming and flush:** The file has no explicit flush call. Response copying is delegated to `httputil.ReverseProxy`. Before serving, `ServeHTTP` calls `http.NewResponseController(w).EnableFullDuplex()`, and on error it only logs. The comment says: "Let the Transport keep reading the request body after the response starts."

